    "OtherAbstract": {
      "Type": "PIP",
      "Language": "eng",
      "AbstractText": "71 women who presented on or after the 6th day following unprotected coitus were fitted with a copper-containing IUD. There were no postcoital contraceptive failures or later method failures in the 64 women who have been followed up. Medical removal due to bleeding, and requests for device removal, reached 46% within 6 months. Delayed postcoital IUD insertion appears to be a safe, effective procedure in skilled hands and may help avoid pregnancy termination."
    }
